    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71785.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, absolutely. You know, we've talked so much about this problem of opioids, and fentanyl is the synthetic opioid that's the biggest killer, and Toledo's had more people die from fentanyl than anything. And finally, we're getting the post office to do this. It should have done years ago, which is to actually screen these packages coming from China, which is where almost all has come from. What's interesting is that the hearing on yesterday on the border to make a switch over to the border is that now fentanyl is also coming up from Mexico over the border. in bigger quantities. Still, most of it's coming from the mail from China, but because we're cracking down on it there, they're now sending it from China to Mexico. They're putting it together in Mexico, sometimes making it into pill form, so it looks like it's an opioid pill, a prescription drug, and then shipping it across the border. So it is all related, as you say, and bottom line is we've got to get at the drug issue by stopping the demand for these drugs, but in the meantime, We got to stop the poison from coming in and at least raise the cost of it on the street because that's one of the big issues. It's so powerful and so inexpensive.",
