    "turn_idx": 17,
    "turn_text": "So Senator, as President Trump is talking about our border crisis and we're looking at the migrant caravans approaching our border from the south and the number of illegal immigrants coming into our country, the opioid crisis, the fentanyl crisis is just a big problem. Would any of the solutions that the Trump administration has proposed, whether it be a border wall, whether it be an increase in the number of CBP and ICE agents on the border, shutting down the border, one of the options that President Trump threw out last week? Would any of those be a solution for the drug crisis in our country?",
