  {
    "episode_id": 71785,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71785.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "It would all help, but ultimately it's about demand. And by the way, I feel the same way about immigration. You know, I've talked about this before. I'm for securing the border. I'm for more fencing. I think President Trump's proposal is right on. But ultimately, if someone can make 10 times as much per hour here than they can make in their home country, they're going to figure out a way to get here over, under, around, through Florida, Canada, whatever. So we have to deal with the demand side of both of those things. If you have the insatiable demand for drugs, and it's so lucrative for these traffickers, they're going to figure out a way to get them in. But again, at a minimum, let's increase the burdens they've got to go through to get here. Let's stop them at the Mexican border. Let's graze the cost of it. so that it's not so inexpensive on the streets. And on immigration, we also obviously need to do it because of the immigration, the drugs, and the trafficking going on there. But on the demand side there, I got to tell you it's jobs, Scott. And I asked these guys yesterday that we had the Border Patrol there, and the Customs and Border Protection guys, and the ICE guys, and I said to all of them, OK, do you believe that the vast majority of these people are coming in for economic reasons to get jobs? And they all said yes. And so what do you do there? Well, you have a program that says you can't get hired in America if you're not legal. And that's the eVerify program that I've talked about before, I think. And I've really been pushing to say, let's come up with a new way where a paid employer, including a small business, can use the technology we've got available to us now to determine, truthfully, whether someone's legal or not. Because right now, you verify that it's out there, it's not mandatory. And even where it's used, people are using fraudulent documents. We can deal with this. It's going to cost a little money to have the right software to be sure you can verify whether someone is the person they say they are on their fake ID. But we should do it, because if you drive the work, then I think you have much better results at the border.",
