    "turn_text": "You are absolutely right, and I have not heard anybody in the media talk about this, but the fact that you got three and a half percent unemployment, the fact you've got wages growing now more than they've grown in the last decade and a half, now that you've got people actually looking for work in higher and higher pay grades, it opens up jobs. And so that's the magnet. And so it is kind of like because of the tax cuts and tax reform and regulatory relief and things that Donald Trump has done to help the economy You do see the economy improving in ways that is making America a better place to come for someone who lives in a poor country where they can't take care of their family. You can't blame them. But they've got to come here legally. And so look, I'm four temporary workers coming. I'm four having legal immigration. But it can't be just floods of illegal immigrants. We've got to figure that out. We're a country of immigration, but we're also a country of laws. And I think you're right. I think the better economy is a big reason for this.",
