    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, it is, and it didn't used to be that way. In fact, as you know, labor unions in particular have always taken a tougher stand on illegal immigration concern that they're taking American jobs that otherwise can be filled by legal Americans. And so the Democrats have usually been at least split on this issue, but now you're right. They seem to have just said forget the laws, you know, just You know, don't enforce the law, don't enforce the border. And you've got to be sure to have a system that's fair. I mean, I'm for that. And you are too. You want to have a legal system that's fair. But you don't want to have a system that doesn't respect law. And by the way, the people who hurt most when you have that kind of a system are people who are Americans, who are at the lower end of the economic scale. And finally, we've got an opportunity for some of these people to come out of the shadows People who have been in and out of jail, people who want to give a second chance, people who have been gone through recovery because they are addicts, and you want to give these people a chance to work. And those are folks that are probably the most impacted by some of the illegal immigration that's coming in. So there's a way to do this. We should continue to be a very generous country. We like legal immigrants. They are enriching our country even today, always have. but it's got to be done in a way that's that legal and regularize",
